gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P3 (S24): "pain" is taken as exceeds in pain felt by the doer himself (do injurers suffer more than the injured) in P3 and as exceeds in pain caused, as the standard measures disgrace (pain to those affected or looking on) where exceeds_pain is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S30) does not follow (gorgias-polus.logic.r3.sense1)
gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C1 (S30): exceeds_evil = F, exceeds_pain = T, exceeds_pain_2 = F, more_disgraceful = T
gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S32): it takes "evil" from evil as harm or badness produced by the act, the standard that measures disgrace to evil as what is worse for the one who does or undergoes it, the sense of Polus's claim that suffering wrong is more evil, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C (S36) does not follow (gorgias-polus.logic.r3.sense2)
gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C (S36): exceeds_evil = T, more_evil = F
